#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c31dcc-393d-54d7-a1d0-1a9b0f4bf516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c31dcc-393d-54d7-a1d0-1a9b0f4bf516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b95e50a-f902-597a-ab12-0718f1ce8489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cbba01bc-4eb3-5032-90e4-0dfde064bcd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316609" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(5,2),(4,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/aef99dd5276166e5c7b4fb2f716b060390b6577f2d3625dd5dc835bcec6c4856.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
